Object-Proto-Cmd

Object::Proto::Cmd is a subcommand CLI framework built on Object::Proto.
Command classes are Object::Proto classes, their attributes become GNU
style command line options, subcommands are registered explicitly, help
text is generated from the declarations and exit codes follow a simple
contract: 0 when fine, 1 when the thing you asked about is wrong, 2 when
the command was used wrongly.

INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc Object::Proto::Cmd

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=Object-Proto-Cmd

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/Object-Proto-Cmd

